2: 
3: **Status:** ✅ Complete  
4: **Created:** 2025-12-06  
5: **Completed:** 2025-12-06  
6: **Effort:** M (1-3 hours)
7: 
8: ---
9: 
10: ## Overview
11: 
12: This document tracks the remaining gaps between the SELECTION_MULTICURSOR.md design and actual implementation. Most multi-cursor features are complete, but several selection operations only work with the primary cursor.
13: 
14: ### Already Implemented ✅
15: 
16: | Feature                                   | Notes                                      |
17: | ----------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------ |
18: | MoveCursorWithSelection (all directions)  | Uses `move_all_cursors_*_with_selection()` |
19: | PageUp/DownWithSelection                  | Multi-cursor aware                         |
20: | MoveCursorWordWithSelection               | Multi-cursor aware                         |
21: | AddCursorAbove/Below                      | Works correctly                            |
22: | ToggleCursorAtPosition                    | Works                                      |
23: | SelectNextOccurrence/SelectAllOccurrences | Works                                      |
24: | Rectangle selection                       | Works                                      |
25: | Expand/ShrinkSelection                    | Single cursor only (acceptable)            |
26: | Multi-cursor editing (insert, delete)     | Uses reverse order, batch undo             |
27: 
28: ### Gaps to Fix ❌
29: 
30: | Feature                            | Location          | Issue                                      |
31: | ---------------------------------- | ----------------- | ------------------------------------------ |
32: | **SelectWord**                     | update.rs:399-441 | Only operates on primary cursor            |
33: | **SelectLine**                     | update.rs:444-467 | Only operates on primary cursor            |
34: | **SelectAll**                      | update.rs:388-396 | Doesn't properly collapse to single cursor |
35: | **ExtendSelectionToPosition**      | update.rs:470-488 | Only extends primary selection             |
36: | **merge_overlapping_selections()** | Not implemented   | Design doc specifies this                  |
37: 
38: ---
39: 
40: ## Design Decisions
41: 
42: Based on Oracle consultation:
43: 
44: | Feature                       | Behavior                                                                              |
45: | ----------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
46: | **SelectAll**                 | Collapse to single cursor + single full-document selection (standard editor behavior) |
47: | **SelectWord**                | Per-cursor word selection → then merge overlapping                                    |
48: | **SelectLine**                | Per-cursor line selection → then merge overlapping                                    |
49: | **ExtendSelectionToPosition** | Collapse to primary cursor first, then extend                                         |
50: | **Expand/ShrinkSelection**    | Keep single-cursor only (complexity not worth it)                                     |
51: 
52: ---
53: 
54: ## Implementation Plan
55: 
56: ### Phase 1: `merge_overlapping_selections()` in EditorState
57: 
58: **Location:** `src/model/editor.rs`
59: 
60: **Algorithm:**
61: 
62: 1. If ≤1 selection, return early
63: 2. Collect `(start, end, index)` tuples for all selections
64: 3. Sort by `start`, then `end`
65: 4. Sweep through and merge if `next.start <= current.end`
66: 5. For merged ranges: `merged_start = min(starts)`, `merged_end = max(ends)`
67: 6. Create canonical forward selections with cursor at `merged_end`
68: 7. Rebuild `cursors` and `selections` vectors
69: 
70: ```rust
71: impl EditorState {
72:     pub fn merge_overlapping_selections(&mut self) {
73:         if self.selections.len() <= 1 {
74:             return;
75:         }
76: 
77:         // 1) Collect (start, end, original_index)
78:         let mut indexed: Vec<(Position, Position, usize)> = self.selections
79:             .iter()
80:             .enumerate()
81:             .map(|(i, s)| (s.start(), s.end(), i))
82:             .collect();
83: 
84:         // 2) Sort by start, then end
85:         indexed.sort_by(|a, b| a.0.cmp(&b.0).then(a.1.cmp(&b.1)));
86: 
87:         // 3) Sweep and merge
88:         let mut merged: Vec<(Position, Position)> = Vec::new();
89:         for (start, end, _) in indexed {
90:             if let Some((_, last_end)) = merged.last_mut() {
91:                 if start <= *last_end {
92:                     // Overlapping or touching - extend
93:                     if end > *last_end {
94:                         *last_end = end;
95:                     }
96:                     continue;
97:                 }
98:             }
99:             merged.push((start, end));
100:         }
101: 
102:         // 4) Rebuild cursors and selections
103:         self.cursors.clear();
104:         self.selections.clear();
105: 
106:         for (start, end) in merged {
107:             self.cursors.push(Cursor::from_position(end));
108:             self.selections.push(Selection::from_positions(start, end));
109:         }
110:     }
111: }
112: ```
113: 
114: **Call sites:**
115: 
116: - After `SelectWord` (when multi-cursor)
117: - After `SelectLine` (when multi-cursor)
118: - Optionally before multi-cursor edits
119: 
120: **Tests:**
121: 
122: - Non-overlapping stays separate: `[0,0..0,3]`, `[0,5..0,7]` → unchanged
123: - Overlapping on same line: `[0,0..0,3]`, `[0,2..0,5]` → `[0,0..0,5]`
124: - Touching (adjacent): `[0,0..0,3]`, `[0,3..0,5]` → `[0,0..0,5]`
125: - Multi-line overlap: `[0,5..1,2]`, `[0,7..2,0]` → `[0,5..2,0]`
126: - Duplicates: two identical → one remains
127: 
128: ---
129: 
130: ### Phase 2: Fix `SelectAll`
131: 
132: **Current behavior:** Uses `cursor_mut()` and `selection_mut()` (primary only)
133: 
134: **New behavior:** Collapse to single cursor + single full-document selection
135: 
136: ```rust
137: EditorMsg::SelectAll => {
138:     let doc = model.document();
139:     let last_line = doc.line_count().saturating_sub(1);
140:     let last_col = doc.line_length(last_line);
141:     let start = Position::new(0, 0);
142:     let end = Position::new(last_line, last_col);
143: 
144:     let editor = model.editor_mut();
145:     editor.cursors.clear();
146:     editor.selections.clear();
147:     editor.cursors.push(Cursor::from_position(end));
148:     editor.selections.push(Selection::from_positions(start, end));
149: 
150:     model.reset_cursor_blink();
151:     Some(Cmd::Redraw)
152: }
153: ```
154: 
155: **Tests:**
156: 
157: - Single cursor → full doc selection
158: - Multiple cursors → collapses to single + full doc selection
159: 
